      "ai_explanation_md": "### Vulnerability Analysis: BOLA on `/orders/{order_id}`\n\n**Severity Rating: Critical (Score: 90/100)**\n\n#### Root Cause\nThe endpoint `/orders/{order_id}` extracts the requested resource identifier from the URL path parameter and retrieves the order object directly from the database without verifying that the `userId` associated with the order matches the `id` of the authenticated user in the `Authorization` bearer token.\n\n#### Impact\nAny authenticated user can enumerate order IDs (e.g. sequentially from 100 to 1000) and dump all customer purchase records across the entire platform, resulting in massive personal and financial data leakage.\n\n#### Remediation (FastAPI / Python)\n```python\n@app.get('/orders/{order_id}')\ndef get_order(order_id: int, current_user = Depends(get_current_user)):\n    order = db.get_order(order_id)\n    if not order:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail='Order not found')\n    if order.user_id != current_user.id and current_user.role != 'admin':\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=403, detail='Forbidden')\n    return order\n```"
    },
